# Normalise line endings: repo uses LF everywhere, on every platform.
# Without this, Windows clients with core.autocrlf=true silently flip
# line endings in the working copy and surface files as "modified" to
# git status even when the content matches the index exactly (observed
# on hf_taipy_app/requirements.txt during the session-45-leftovers
# cleanup — it had been flagged modified for multiple cycles with no
# actual content change).
#
# `text=auto` lets Git auto-detect binary vs text; `eol=lf` forces LF
# for anything Git classifies as text in BOTH the index and the working
# copy. Binary files are unaffected.

* text=auto eol=lf
